{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1414231-what\u2019s-the-difference-between-a-mantle-and-an-incarnation","id":1414231,"title":"What\u2019s the difference between a Mantle and an Incarnation?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Onyx Path Worlds","Scion"],"posts":[{"date":"2020-09-17T10:54:16-07:00","id":1414231,"title":"What\u2019s the difference between a Mantle and an Incarnation?","content":"I think I get it but I just need someone to explain it again to me so I can make sure.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-17T11:35:33-07:00","id":1414237,"title":"","content":"A Mantle is a bit of mythology that derives from Legend and determines how Fatebinding works: what sorts of stories does the God excel in? An Incarnation is a physical manifestation of a God that he or she can use to physically interact with the World.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-17T15:20:43-07:00","id":1414274,"title":"","content":"Thank you.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-17T17:47:36-07:00","id":1414303,"title":"","content":"I'll add that my impression is that when a god Incarnates, it may be with the intention (or unintentional result) of creating a new Mantel. <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-18T04:42:43-07:00","id":1414352,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>No One of Consequence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1414231-what\u2019s-the-difference-between-a-mantle-and-an-incarnation?p=1414303#post1414303\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'll add that my impression is that when a god Incarnates, it may be with the intention (or unintentional result) of creating a new Mantel. <br /></div> </div> </div> </div>I understand. Thanks.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-18T10:37:46-07:00","id":1414419,"title":"","content":"I saw a metaphor I like, for Mantles.<br /> <br /> Think of a Mantle as a role in a play or a tv show. We know roughly what James Bond does, but some aspects may shift as the Mantle is carried by another.<br /> <br /> But they're all Bond.<br /> <br /> Incarnation, as mentioned, is when a God decides to visit the World without going full glory.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-18T12:12:06-07:00","id":1414438,"title":"","content":"So like a Mantle is like different actors playing the same role?<br /> <br /> Thank you! Now I totally get it.<br /> <br /> What about Krishna and Rama from the Deva pantheon? Are they Mantles or Incarnations of Vishnu?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-18T12:40:50-07:00","id":1414446,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Penelope</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1414231-what\u2019s-the-difference-between-a-mantle-and-an-incarnation?p=1414438#post1414438\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So like a Mantle is like different actors playing the same role?</div> </div> </div> </div>Not exactly.<br /> <br /> Think a Mantle like a role in a play, the gods are actors, many can play the same role, or the same actor can play many roles. But the gods kind of Own the roles, and can share or borrow or lose the mantles of play it wrong. Matos are not small roles, they are protagonist roles, worth of titles. A god without a mantle has no role in the play and can\u2019t act, basically, unless he can create a new role or take someone\u2019s else role.<br /> <br /> Now the Incarnatios are the way gods manifest in the world, like when we play a character in a RPG, they character is the manifestation of the player in the world of the game, but it\u2019s not the player and the player is not the character. Sometimes the gods create versions of themselves just to play for a while, sometimes they create a baby and play that role until it grows up and live their own adventures.<br /> <br /> If the god play the incarnation for long enough and create his own story, he probably can create a new mantle for himself.<br /> <br /> On Rama and Krishna, as far as I understand, one is one of many incarnations of the other, that played so well that created a mantle. What I don\u2019t know is if they work as independent persons, a multiple personality syndrome of a person that can be in multiple places at same time or if they are the same person pretending to be many.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":24985,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","user":"Mateus Luz","date":". 09-18-2020, 03:43 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-18T14:22:03-07:00","id":1414466,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24020-mateus\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar24020_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"24020\" data-vbnamecard=\"24020\">Mateus</a> Luz Thank you. That definitely helps.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-18T19:51:14-07:00","id":1414500,"title":"","content":"How many gods have worn the Mantle of &quot;the Doctor?&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-18T20:16:55-07:00","id":1414502,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Astromancer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1414231-what\u2019s-the-difference-between-a-mantle-and-an-incarnation?p=1414500#post1414500\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How many gods have worn the Mantle of &quot;the Doctor?&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Well there was that one time when he actively stepped away from his Mantle and name-<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-01T05:02:49-07:00","id":1416228,"title":"","content":"Sorry to hijack this thread but is a mantle in Scion 2nd basically what an avatar was in 1st?<br /> <br /> Back then we used to display a different avatar for let's say different kinds of followers, to arrive before them as they imagine you?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26156-avalontzi","name":"AvalonTzi","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-01T05:33:19-07:00","id":1416234,"title":"","content":"Not sure. Not really familiar with 1e. Maybe someone else will know.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-01T06:08:40-07:00","id":1416239,"title":"","content":"No. 1e had 3 things called avatar, and none of them are Mantle, the manifestation of a god (probably going to keep this name, and the one you are referring to), the ultimate power of a purview and the personalities of a Titan.<br /> <br /> Your example is kind of how it works, but a Mantle is more than just what you look like, it\u2019s a personality that can be borrowed and shared, because gods are not mortals. A Mantle shapes a god when they use it, for example, when Ares is Mars he loses the barbarian aspect and gain a general one, he can\u2019t manifest the general aspect when Ares is the mantle being worn, it\u2019s like if he never had it, same for Mars and the barbarian aspect.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-01T06:15:21-07:00","id":1416242,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mateus Luz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1414231-what\u2019s-the-difference-between-a-mantle-and-an-incarnation?p=1416239#post1416239\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No. 1e had 3 things called avatar, and none of them are Mantle, the manifestation of a god (probably going to keep this name, and the one you are referring to), the ultimate power of a purview and the personalities of a Titan.<br /> <br /> Your example is kind of how it works, but a Mantle is more than just what you look like, it\u2019s a personality that can be borrowed and shared, because gods are not mortals. A Mantle shapes a god when they use it, for example, when Ares is Mars he loses the barbarian aspect and gain a general one, he can\u2019t manifest the general aspect when Ares is the mantle being worn, it\u2019s like if he never had it, same for Mars and the barbarian aspect.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ok, many helpful answers in this thread already but yours made something click in my brain. <br /> <br /> Thank you very much. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26156-avalontzi","name":"AvalonTzi","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-01T09:12:29-07:00","id":1416278,"title":"","content":"Yeah, think of a Mantle as the identity or fingerprint of a God. The quick &quot;Oh yes, I know that they're about&quot; thing when you hear Thor. Like, you know, roughly, what Thor does and who he is.<br /> <br /> &quot;Oh yeah, Thor. Rides a chariot with goats, has a big hammer, thunder guy, fights giants&quot;<br /> <br /> You know, roughly, what Thor is about, what he does. THAT is the Mantle of Thor. One can try to claim the Mantle of Thor by, essentially, trying to be a better Thor than Thor. You'll need a big hammer and you'll need to fight a lot of giants, but you can (to use the Elder Scrolls quote) walk like Thor until Thor must walk like you.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-01T10:43:12-07:00","id":1416297,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kyman201</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1414231-what\u2019s-the-difference-between-a-mantle-and-an-incarnation?p=1416278#post1416278\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, think of a Mantle as the identity or fingerprint of a God. The quick &amp;quot;Oh yes, I know that they're about&amp;quot; thing when you hear Thor. Like, you know, roughly, what Thor does and who he is.<br /> <br /> &amp;quot;Oh yeah, Thor. Rides a chariot with goats, has a big hammer, thunder guy, fights giants&amp;quot;<br /> <br /> You know, roughly, what Thor is about, what he does. THAT is the Mantle of Thor. One can try to claim the Mantle of Thor by, essentially, trying to be a better Thor than Thor. You'll need a big hammer and you'll need to fight a lot of giants, but you can (to use the Elder Scrolls quote) walk like Thor until Thor must walk like you.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thanks. This post is really helpful.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-02T23:52:31-07:00","id":1416590,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kyman201</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1414231-what\u2019s-the-difference-between-a-mantle-and-an-incarnation?p=1416278#post1416278\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, think of a Mantle as the identity or fingerprint of a God. The quick &quot;Oh yes, I know that they're about&quot; thing when you hear Thor. Like, you know, roughly, what Thor does and who he is.<br /> <br /> &quot;Oh yeah, Thor. Rides a chariot with goats, has a big hammer, thunder guy, fights giants&quot;<br /> <br /> You know, roughly, what Thor is about, what he does. THAT is the Mantle of Thor. One can try to claim the Mantle of Thor by, essentially, trying to be a better Thor than Thor. You'll need a big hammer and you'll need to fight a lot of giants, but you can (to use the Elder Scrolls quote) walk like Thor until Thor must walk like you.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> There's nothing about that entire post that I don't seriously dig on. Especially the last paragraph. Well written <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2608-squee","name":"Squee","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2608_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"120"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-03T16:02:50-07:00","id":1416652,"title":"","content":"The Mantle is the character sheet a God uses as a God. The Incarnation is a God LARPing as a mortal.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":561,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/561-mockery","user":"Mockery","date":". 10-05-2020, 05:57 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/561-mockery","name":"Mockery","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar561_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"876"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}